#: ../../source/docs/common-resoluteh7.rst:93
#: 6788cc22f7c64721ac6820b324f6ee47
msgid "Compass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-resoluteh7.rst:95
#: 9329cf72382147c783c52cb4d40f122a
msgid "The Resolute H7 does not have a builtin compass, but you can attach an external compass using I2C on the SDA and SCL pads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-resoluteh7.rst:98
#: a58bd5b0b53149ebbd9d5fc6c3390ab6
msgid "Camera control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-resoluteh7.rst:100
#: 309a1601d21e4ef2a404ac3fcbb581bb
msgid "GPIO 82 controls the camera output to the connectors marked \"CAM1\" and \"CAM2\". Setting this GPIO low switches the video output from CAM1 to CAM2. By default RELAY3 is configured to control this pin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-resoluteh7.rst:103
#: 98a4baacd7d44c05a93e416ed4e0c596
msgid "VTX Power Control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-resoluteh7.rst:105
#: 000e977c7ba74bc58959f67ed16fc210
msgid "GPIO 81 provides on/off control of the 12V supply. RELAY 2 controls this GPIO"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-resoluteh7.rst:108
#: 8dc0ff69fe514020984d41863c7b2eba
msgid "HD VTX connector"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-resoluteh7.rst:110
#: 8432aea405c346a3a924328267568fc6
msgid "When using HD video transmission, the flight controller needs to connect to DJI TX and RX via Serial 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-resoluteh7.rst:113
#: ff9f795ba7c04eefae7da3b5e34882fd
msgid "OSD Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-resoluteh7.rst:115
#: b5af43d2a2ed4d2b83410a25184ed39d
msgid "The Resolute H7 has an onboard OSD using a MAX7456 chip and is enabled by default. The CAM1/2 and VTX pins provide connections for using the internal OSD. Simultaneous DisplayPort OSD is also possible and is configured by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-resoluteh7.rst:118
#: 24a49466984a46a694c193da5f6c3772
msgid "Loading Firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-resoluteh7.rst:120
#: 64dbcf7a987a4e908fe677a2be4c9dde
msgid "Firmware for these boards can be found `here <https://firmware.ardupilot.org>`__ in sub-folders labeled \"ResoluteH7\". Initial firmware load can be done with DFU by plugging in USB with the bootloader button pressed. Then you should load the \"with_bl.hex\" firmware, using your favorite DFU loading tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-resoluteh7.rst:125
#: d68998042d24423ab16f3bec39593618
msgid "Once the initial firmware is loaded you can update the firmware using any ArduPilot ground station software. Updates should be done with the \\*.apj firmware files."
msgstr ""
